{
  format: 1
  name: update-seed-root-singleton-applies-if-absent
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#modules", "§13.13", "#state-model", "§8.2", "#package-structure", "§4.1", "#loading", "§9.2"]
  note: '''
    §13.13's `$seed` rule is scoped by ADDRESS and names no container: "A seed
    value applies only where its address holds no current value... An existing
    row, field, or member is never modified by `$seed`". §8.2 makes a writable
    non-collection root member durable state at its own address, and §4.1 lets
    `$seed` supply it — so both directions of the rule hold at the root exactly as
    they do for a keyed row. This is the `$seed` half of the seam whose `$bundle`
    half is pinned by `09-loading-bootstrap/update-bundle-root-singleton-merge`.

    One `host_load` from 1.0.0 to 1.1.0 (a compatible minor, §9.2/§20.1) covers
    both directions at once:
      - theme:  seeded at genesis and then EDITED locally to "mine"; the 1.1.0
                seed re-declares it as "T2". The address holds a current value,
                so the seed does not touch it and "mine" survives;
      - motto:  absent at 1.0.0 and never written, so its address holds nothing
                after the §20.1 carry; the 1.1.0 seed supplies it, and the value
                is INSERTED ("M2").

    Both members are optional (`text?`), so an absent one is admissible state
    (§5.1) and the case isolates the apply-if-absent rule rather than required
    member admission.
  '''

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.seedsing@1.0.0"
    $model: {
      motto: "text?"
      theme: "text?"
      $mut: {
        set_theme: [
          ".theme = @v"
          "return . { theme }"
        ]
      }
      $public: {
        settings: {
          $view: ". { motto, theme }"
          $mut: { set_theme: ".set_theme" }
        }
      }
    }
    $seed: { theme: "T1" }
  }

  steps: [
    // Genesis (§13.13): `$seed` applies as an ordinary insert.
    { watch: "public.settings", id: "w0"
      expect_init: { value: { motto: "$absent", theme: "T1" } } }
    // User data now occupies the seeded singleton address.
    { call: "public.settings.set_theme", args: { v: "mine" }
      expect: { outcome: ok, value: { theme: "mine" } } }
    { host_load: {
        package: {
          $liasse: 1
          $app: "t.seedsing@1.1.0"
          $model: {
            motto: "text?"
            theme: "text?"
            $mut: {
              set_theme: [
                ".theme = @v"
                "return . { theme }"
              ]
            }
            $public: {
              settings: {
                $view: ". { motto, theme }"
                $mut: { set_theme: ".set_theme" }
              }
            }
          }
          $seed: { theme: "T2", motto: "M2" }
        }
      }
      expect: { outcome: ok, result: committed } }
    { watch: "public.settings", id: "w1"
      expect_init: { value: { motto: "M2", theme: "mine" } } }
  ]
}
